title: searchStart
position: 142,462
---
You choose to walk down memory lane.
You open up the desk, and see\:
Several bottles of different colored inks, used for your artistic pursuits.
A suspiciously old Whiskerbar, half-eaten.
A homemade thumb piano from your grandmother.
Various loose papers, worn on all edges.
A pocket mirror, encased in lilac cloth.
...and some other stuff.
<<jump searchOptions>>
<<set $searched = true>>
===

title: searchOptions
position: 16,16
---
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Ink bottles
        Bottles of every color, including black, red, blue, and that's it really. 
        You think ink is the coolest form of artistic expression. Everyone can see something different in it.
        You remember painting a sick ass tree down by the river, and your mom thought it was a wet bird.
        Some things may be more objective than others.
        <<jump searchOptions>>
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Questionable Whiskerbar
        A wonderful combination of fish, peanut butter, and molasses.
        People usually only eat half, because their mouth is glued shut after the first bite.
        Your teeth have never forgiven you. Your stomach was quite happy though.
        You leave the bar to marinate. //cool text effect on marinate
        <<jump searchOptions>>
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Piano for Thumbs
        Made out of a piece of driftwood and some tender metal. Cracked at the edge.
        You think your grandmother got it for you in an attempt to encourage a sense of musicality.
        You think a guitar or flute would've been cooler.
        Or maybe a vibraphone...
        <<jump searchOptions>>
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Papers
        Old mail, birthday cards, the errant bad drawing.
        Sometimes you use them as palettes for your ink.
        You used to use your desk for that, but started losing track of your black, red, and blue possesions.
        Oh desk, the great devourer of pens and markers alike.
        <<jump searchOptions>>
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Mirror 
        You unwrap the mirror and see yourself.
        Harte, an Otter, 18. An artist of some sort. Restless.
        You like fish and rebellious music.
        You don't think you would ever rebel against much, though. 
        Your whiskers are freshly whisked.
        Your tail is freshly a tail.
        Everything in its right place.
        <<jump searchOptions>>
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Stop Looking
        You close the desk, having utilized your curiosity. 
